  "Question": "The expression \\(81^{-(2^{-2})}\\) has the same value as:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac1{81}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)",
    "C": "\\(3\\)",
    "D": "\\(81\\)",
    "E": "\\(81^4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First evaluate the power inside the parentheses:\n\\[\n2^{-2}=\\frac{1}{2^2}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nThe exponent on \\(81\\) is therefore \\(-1/4\\). A negative exponent takes the reciprocal, and an exponent of \\(1/4\\) takes the positive fourth root. Since \\(3^4=81\\),\n\\[\n81^{-(2^{-2})}=81^{-1/4}\n=\\frac{1}{81^{1/4}}=\\boxed{\\frac13},\n\\]\nchoice B.",
